{"candidates":[{"claim":"The batch criticism mechanism fails to retire rival positions because coverage debt grows superlinearly (O(N^2)) with the number of accepted rivals, exhausting the criticism token budget. An optimization utilizing ensemble methods (directed research: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ensemble_learning) to weight and prioritize disanalogies would reduce coverage debt to near-linear growth and restore retirement dynamics.","counterconditions":["If the accepted rivals are highly redundant, the combinatorial explosion is illusory and simple linear coverage would suffice.","If ensemble criticism fails to satisfy the normative dependence-ref requirements of SRC_004, it may be rejected by the formal harness (SRC_007).","If the failure to retire rivals is due to a lack of ground truth rather than budget exhaustion, ensemble voting will not identify the correct rivals to retire."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"Per SRC_001's budget-pressure causal loop, as accepted rivals grow from 18 to 60, the requirement to generate per-target warrants for every pair creates a combinatorial explosion of coverage debt. The criticism-weighted attention becomes saturated and fails to retire positions. By treating each criticism as a weak learner in an ensemble method that votes on the retirement of specific rivals, the limited attention budget is concentrated on the most vulnerable rivals, overcoming the coverage bottleneck.","optional_refs":["ba687c5f145e404c53a84549cf366e0b6e0106eec67404c07231357fed09e672","08d0b004073ba6e72194b12e4f73e88c663a4000aec863f510bbdf189e93b039"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":["ba687c5f145e404c53a84549cf366e0b6e0106eec67404c07231357fed09e672","08d0b004073ba6e72194b12e4f73e88c663a4000aec863f510bbdf189e93b039"],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.65}],"simulation_proposals":[]}